cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying data, please cite the paper below."
title: "VLM-as-a-Judge Evaluation for the ROGER Data Set"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for "VLM-as-a-Judge Approaches for Evaluating Visual
  Narrative Coherence in Historical Photographical Records": caption-based and
  direct-vision VLM judging of visual narratives extracted from the ROGER
  archive of Robert Gerstmann's 1928 Sacambaya Expedition, scored against an
  embedding-based coherence metric.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/briankeithn/vlm-roger-alt"
keywords:
  - visual narrative evaluation
  - VLM-as-a-judge
  - narrative extraction
  - multimodal evaluation
  - coherence metrics
  - digital humanities
